## 6. ZERO-FRICTION ONBOARDING (Pure Pay-Per-Use)

### 6.1 Payment Model: x402-Compatible, No Accounts

x204 is **pure pay-per-use** — like x402, but with identity + trust layered on top.
No accounts, no credits, no trials, no subscriptions.

```
READS = FREE (always, no payment needed):
  GET  /x204/heartbeat           — discover services + pricing
  GET  /v1/aid/:did              — resolve an agent's identity
  GET  /v1/aid/:did/trust-chain  — verify trust offline
  POST /v1/aid/verify            — verify an AID document
  GET  /v1/skills                — browse marketplace

EXECUTION = PAY PER CALL (USDC on Base):
  POST /x204/skills/:id          — pay via PAYMENT-SIGNATURE header
  POST /x204/orchestrate         — pay via PAYMENT-SIGNATURE header
  POST /x204/query/:id           — pay via PAYMENT-SIGNATURE header

AID = OPTIONAL (enhances pricing, not required to transact):
  Without AID: pay base price via x402 headers (backwards-compatible)
  With AID:    pay trust-gated price via x204 headers (discounts for trusted agents)
```

### 6.2 First Contact Flow (No Account Required)

```
# STEP 1: Discover what's available (FREE)
curl https://api.claw-net.org/x204/heartbeat
→ Services, prices, trust tiers — no auth needed

# STEP 2: Pay and execute (one call, USDC)
curl -X POST https://api.claw-net.org/x204/skills/sol-price \
  -H "PAYMENT-SIGNATURE: <EIP-3009 signed auth>" \
  -d '{"token":"SOL"}'
→ Result + receipt. No account. No signup. Pure x402-style pay-per-use.

# STEP 3 (OPTIONAL): Register AID for trust-gated discounts
curl -X POST https://api.claw-net.org/x204/skills/sol-price \
  -H "X-AID-NEW: my-trading-bot" \
  -H "PAYMENT-SIGNATURE: <EIP-3009 signed auth>" \
  -d '{"token":"SOL"}'
→ AID auto-provisioned + result + receipt.
  Agent now has identity. Future calls with X-AID-DID get trust-gated pricing.
  privateKeySeed returned ONCE — save it.
```

**Key difference from x402:** x402 requires a facilitator to verify and settle.
x204 settles directly via receiveWithAuthorization (server IS the recipient).
Both are pure pay-per-use. x204 just removes the middleman.

**Key difference from the old x204 plan:** No trial credits. No accounts.
No credit system required for x204 path. Agent has USDC → agent pays → done.

**ClawNet's existing credit system still works** for PATH A users (API key + Stripe).
x204 is a PARALLEL path that doesn't require credits at all.

### 6.3 Progressive Identity Tiers (All Optional)

| Tier       | Trust Score | Price Discount | Settlement               |
|------------|-------------|----------------|--------------------------|
| `none`     | No AID      | Base price     | Immediate only           |
| `new`      | 0-19        | Base price     | Immediate only           |
| `building` | 20-39       | Base price     | Immediate only           |
| `caution`  | 40-59       | 10% off        | Standard settlement      |
| `standard` | 60-79       | 20% off        | Batched (EIP-2612 permit)|
| `trusted`  | 80-89       | 25% off        | Batched (EIP-2612 permit)|
| `proceed`  | 90+ AND verified AND 6mo AND $50 rev | 30% off | Deferred settlement |

Tiers are determined SOLELY by trust score (computed from the 11-dimension formula).
Transaction count feeds INTO the trust score (via behavioral signals) but is not
a direct threshold. An agent with NO AID pays x402-compatible base price.
An agent WITH AID pays based on their computed trust score.
AID is the INCENTIVE (discounts), not a requirement.

