### 39.11 Trust Oscillation Defense

**Attack:** Agent alternates good/bad behavior, locks in high tier every other window.

**Rule:** Tier assignment uses trailing 3-window average, not point-in-time snapshot.
If score crossed a tier boundary downward in ANY of the last 3 windows → assign
the LOWER tier. Takes 3 consecutive good windows to recover.

### 39.12 Merkle Snapshot Timing Randomization

**Attack:** Time positive attestations just before known snapshot cutoff.

**Rule:** Snapshot runs every 4 hours with ±15 minute random jitter.
Cutoff time is not predictable. Attestation clustering just before any
fixed time window has no guaranteed effect.

